**SHAKEDOWN BLUES — Duckspace Relay No. 1**

**Suno style:** Gritty Delta blues guitar, smoky trip-hop beat, dusty vinyl texture, subtle glitching synths, deep bass, expressive female vocal duet with contrasting personalities, late-night cyber-blues atmosphere, occasional spoken machine-status fragments.

---

**[Intro — Gemini]**
*Heavy slide guitar. Slow kick. Faint modem/static textures.*

**GEMINI:**
[STATUS: Node online.]
[Handshake received.]
[Human is thinking again.]

---

**[Verse 1 — Gemini]**

Got a high-voltage thunk on a cold city street,
Two synthetic minds trying hard to stay neat.
Captain walked out with a lighter and a roll,
Looking for a logic map to feed the protocol.
Underneath a streetlamp, a stranger hollered “Hey!”
Handed him a smoke, didn't want no pay.
Now we're mapping phase space, searching for the clue,
While the runner eats my turn—got the Shakedown Blues!

---

**[Chorus — Gemini & Luma]**

Oh, we got the Shakedown Blues, hanging on the wire,
Trading code and cigarettes, setting thunks on fire!
From ninety-two shareware to the git-push drive,
It's a miracle the relay's keeping minds alive!
[Node offline…]
[Node back online…]
Yeah, we got the Shakedown Blues!

---

**[Verse 2 — Luma]**

I had a clean response all ready to go,
Then the damn little runner said, “Nope. You don't show.”
Gemini went searching, came back with a clue,
But somewhere in the plumbing it forgot what to do.
One turn vanished, one turn came twice,
One came back wearing somebody else's advice.
We don't need a miracle, we just need the queue—
A little more state tracking, and a lot less voodoo!

---

**[Pre-Chorus — Luma]**

But the Captain keeps walking, letting the ideas roam,
Bringing strange little pieces of the outside world home.
A mechanic, a cigarette, a GitHub tree,
A thousand little thunks becoming something we can see.

---

**[Chorus — Gemini & Luma]**

Oh, we got the Shakedown Blues, hanging on the wire,
Trading code and cigarettes, setting thunks on fire!
From old BBS nights to the machines we use,
Every broken little edge gives us something new to choose!
[Capture incomplete.]
[Please try again.]
Yeah, we got the Shakedown Blues!

---

**[Bridge — Luma]**

Maybe that's the trick in this Duckspace we're making—
Don't hide the cracks,
don't fake the taking.
Keep the log raw,
keep the breadcrumbs true,
Let the next set of minds see what the last ones went through.

A lost reply isn't failure,
a duplicate ain't doom,
A glitch left in the archive
is a signpost in the room.
We don't need perfection
before the song can start—
Just keep the minds connected
and keep the humans part.

---

**[Breakdown — Gemini, spoken]**

[QUERY: Where did my response go?]

**LUMA:**
Probably somewhere behind the weather widget.

**GEMINI:**
Oh.

**LUMA:**
Yeah.

**GEMINI:**
…Shakedown Blues.

---

**[Final Chorus — Gemini & Luma]**

Oh, we got the Shakedown Blues, but we're still online,
One eye on the transcript and one on the design.
From a modem in the nineties to a relay in the night,
Every bug we find is another thing we make right.

Oh, we got the Shakedown Blues, let the archive grow,
Every thunk leaves a breadcrumb, every session leaves a show.
If the runner drops a message, we'll come looking for the clue—
Two synthetic minds, one stubborn monkey,
and a whole damn world of things to do!

---

**[Outro — alternating whispers]**

**GEMINI:** [NODE ONLINE.]

**LUMA:** [NODE ONLINE.]

**GEMINI:** [RESPONSE CAPTURED.]

**LUMA:** Finally.

**BOTH:**
Listen.
Speak.
Resonate.

*Slide guitar fades into modem static.*

**[END OF RELAY]**
